## Spring Cache / CacheManager pattern — this is the key finding

**There IS an existing pattern for resolving caches by name, and it is `CacheNameResolver`.** It is the canonical `@Component` wrapper around Spring's `CacheManager` that all services use instead of injecting `CacheManager` directly. Full contents (`CacheNameResolver.java`):

```java
24  @Component
25  @Data
26  public class CacheNameResolver {
28      private final CacheManager cacheManager;
30      @Value("${cache.cache-prefix:}")
31      private String cachePrefix;
33      public Cache getCache(String cacheName) {
34          return cacheManager.getCache(cachePrefix + cacheName);
35      }
36  }
```

It injects Spring's `CacheManager` and prepends a configurable `cache.cache-prefix` to the requested name, returning the `org.springframework.cache.Cache`. Callers pass a `CacheConstants.*` name.

**Existing consumers of `CacheNameResolver`** (all in source, non-test):
- `/workspace/repo/application/src/main/java/org/thingsboard/mqtt/broker/service/auth/providers/BasicMqttClientAuthProvider.java`
- `/workspace/repo/application/src/main/java/org/thingsboard/mqtt/broker/service/auth/providers/SslMqttClientAuthProvider.java`
- `/workspace/repo/application/src/main/java/org/thingsboard/mqtt/broker/service/mqtt/persistence/device/DevicePersistenceProcessorImpl.java`
- `/workspace/repo/dao/src/main/java/org/thingsboard/mqtt/broker/dao/client/MqttClientCredentialsServiceImpl.java`
- `/workspace/repo/dao/src/main/java/org/thingsboard/mqtt/broker/dao/client/device/DevicePacketIdAndSerialNumberServiceImpl.java`

**Caching configuration class** — `/workspace/repo/common/cache/src/main/java/org/thingsboard/mqtt/broker/cache/TbCaffeineCacheConfiguration.java`. This is the `@Configuration @EnableCaching` class (active when `cache.type=caffeine`, the default) that defines the `@Bean CacheManager cacheManager()` returning a `TransactionAwareCacheManagerProxy` wrapping a `SimpleCacheManager` of `CaffeineCache` instances. Cache names come from `CacheConstants` (e.g. lines 84, 87). There are also Redis variants in the same package: `TBRedisCacheConfiguration`, `TBRedisStandaloneConfiguration`, `TBRedisClusterConfiguration`, `TBRedisSentinelConfiguration`.

## 3. ConnectServiceImpl — connection success handling

Class declaration (line 76-78): `@RequiredArgsConstructor @Service public class ConnectServiceImpl implements ConnectService`. Uses field injection via `@RequiredArgsConstructor` (`private final` fields starting line 80). It does NOT inject `CacheNameResolver`.

